  "id": "css.panels-dialogs",
  "title": "Panels, dialogs and light layer",
  "summary": "Control and dialog stylesheet set: panels.css (layers, brushes, props, group tabs, dock, menu), dialogs.css (scrim, dialog, prefs, toast, numpop, toggles), no-scrollbar rules, Inter and JetBrains Mono font imports, and the light-mode shadow layer.",
  "description": "Five sheets loaded after `tokens.css` and `shell.css`. `dialogs.css` holds `.cv-scrim`/`.cv-dialog` (the dialog kit), the toggle switch, number popover and Preferences chrome; `panels.css` holds the panel group, dock, float and glass menu rules; `scrollbars.css` removes every scrollbar (owner rule); `fonts.css` imports Inter 400/500/600 and JetBrains Mono 400/700 from @fontsource; `light-mode.css` only restores the glass shadow under `body.theme-light`. `panels.css` still has four raw local-stacking z-index values (2, 4, 5) at this commit; everything above local stacking uses the scale. Many class families are formvis-specific (layers, brushes, filters) and are dropped on a port.",
  "kind": "style",
  "layer": "frontend",
